From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kurt Kiefer <kkiefer@nvidia.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc/tegra: pmc: Add Tegra264 scratch register offsets

The linux-noble commit f26de42a861ec (Idb9534ea, gerrit 3456564) added
boot-chain sysfs infrastructure across three files: pmc.c, tegra264-pmc.c,
and pmc.h.  When ported to linux-stable as 5f33ed96ac440, only the pmc.c
hunk landed; the tegra264-pmc.c hunk that sets scratch_l0_1_0=0x67C and
scratch_l0_21_0=0x6cc was dropped.  On linux-stable the unified pmc.c
handles all SoCs so there is no separate tegra264-pmc.c to carry these
values.  Add them directly to tegra264_pmc_regs.

Upstream-Status: Backport [tegra264-pmc.c hunk of linux-noble
  f26de42a861ec (Idb9534ea, gerrit 3456564) dropped in linux-stable
  5f33ed96ac440; offsets folded into tegra264_pmc_regs in pmc.c]
Signed-off-by: Kurt Kiefer <kkiefer@nvidia.com>

diff --git a/drivers/soc/tegra/pmc.c b/drivers/soc/tegra/pmc.c
index 11682a9f4dd9c..d4c57e5ec9517 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/tegra/pmc.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/tegra/pmc.c
@@ -4870,6 +4870,8 @@ static const struct tegra_pmc_regs tegra264_pmc_regs = {
 	.rst_level_mask = 0x3,
 	.aowake_mask_w = 0x200,
 	.aowake_status_w = 0x410,
+	.scratch_l0_1_0 = 0x67c,
+	.scratch_l0_21_0 = 0x6cc,
 	.aowake_status_r = 0x610,
 	.aowake_tier2_routing = 0x660,
 	.aowake_sw_status_w = 0x624,
-- 
2.43.0

